.TH VOMD 1 "" "VOMD" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vomd \- view Markdown documents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vomd
.RB [ \-\-no\-settings ]
.RI [ FILE ]
.br
.B vomd
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vomd
(View-Only Markdown) opens a Markdown document for reading: CommonMark and GitHub Flavored
Markdown, in light and dark themes that follow the system.
It never edits files and never runs HTML.
.PP
Any extension is read as Markdown.
With
.I FILE
given as
.BR \- ,
the document is read from standard input.
With no
.IR FILE ,
an empty window opens:
.B Ctrl+O
picks a file to open, or one can be dropped on it (X11).
Each window is its own process.
.PP
The document is reloaded when it changes on disk and the window gets focus, keeping the
reading position.
Remote images are not loaded until asked for (\fBI\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-settings
Ignore the settings file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.RB "Wheel, " Up ", " Down ", " j ", " k
Scroll.
.TP
.BR PgUp ", " PgDn ", " Space ", " Shift+Space
Scroll a page.
.TP
.BR Home ", " End ", " g ", " G
Top, bottom.
.TP
.BR [ ", " ]
Previous, next heading.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+= ", " Ctrl+\- ", " Ctrl+0 ", Ctrl+wheel"
Zoom in, out, reset.
.TP
.B T
Theme: system, light, dark.
.TP
.B B
Show or hide the toolbar.
.TP
.B C
Show or hide the contents panel: the document's headings at the window's left, with the one being
read marked.
A click on a heading jumps to it, as a link to its anchor does, and the wheel over the panel
scrolls the panel.
In a window at least 740 logical pixels wide the panel sits beside the document; in a narrower one
it covers the document's edge, and a click on a heading or on the document closes it.
The
.B toc
setting starts with the panel open.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Find in the document.
A bar below the toolbar takes what is typed, and every match is marked in the text, the current one
more strongly, with its place among the matches ("3 / 17") in the bar.
While the bar is open the letter keys are text, Backspace deletes, and
.BR Enter ", " F3 " and " Ctrl+G
go to the next match and with Shift to the previous.
A short selection of one line is the query when the bar opens.
.B Esc
or the bar's close button closes it.
.TP
.B W
Wide layout on or off: the text spans the window instead of stopping at
.BR line_width .
.TP
.B I
Load the remote images of this document (again to hide them).
.TP
.BR R ", " F5
Reload.
.TP
Drag
Select text.
A drag that starts on a link selects, and does not follow it.
Dragging past the top or bottom of the window scrolls.
.TP
.RB "Double-click, triple-click, " Shift "+click"
Select a word, a block (a paragraph, heading, code block or table row), or extend the selection.
.TP
Click the copy button of a code block
Copy the block's code to the clipboard, as written (no language tag, no quote marks or list
indent, no line break after the last line).
The button shows at the block's upper right while the pointer is over the block, and a check mark
for two seconds after the copy.
It leaves the selection alone, and does not set the primary selection.
.TP
.B Ctrl+A
Select everything.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+C ", " Ctrl+Insert
Copy the selection to the clipboard, as plain text.
The selection made with the mouse (or by Ctrl+A) is also offered as the primary selection, which
a middle click pastes (X11 and Wayland); the
.B primary_selection
setting turns that off.
.TP
.BR Backspace ", " Alt+Left ", " Ctrl+[
Back, after following a link to another document.
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open a file, in the desktop's file dialog (the portal's, else
.BR zenity (1)
or
.BR kdialog (1)),
so a bare window manager needs one of them installed.
.TP
.B Esc
Close the toolbar's menu if it is open, else the find bar, else the contents panel if it covers the
document, else clear the selection, else quit.
.TP
.BR Q ", " Ctrl+W
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vomd/settings.ini
Optional settings
.RI ( ~/.config/vomd/settings.ini
by default): plain
.I key = value
lines, applied when the window gets focus.
The toolbar's settings button creates it with every key listed and commented out.
Theme, zoom, toolbar, contents panel, wide layout and window size are saved when they change.
.SH PRIVACY
.B vomd
makes no network requests of its own.
Remote images are fetched with the system
.BR curl (1)
only after
.B I
is pressed for a document, or for every document with
.BR "remote_images = always" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://github.com/allenguarnes/vomd
.UE
